## Why This Is Asked

This question probes data governance, access control, and incident response fundamentals for beginner CISSP candidates, with a realistic data-import scenario.

## Key Concepts

- Data classification and handling
- RBAC/ABAC and just-in-time access
- Data provenance and SBOM concepts
- Encryption at rest and in transit; KMS/key rotation
- Immutable audit logging and incident response/testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Validate payload schema and attach a signed attestation
function validateAndSign(payload, signer) {
  // simple schema check
  if (!payload || !payload.data) throw new Error('Invalid');
  const attestation = signer.sign(JSON.stringify(payload));
  return { payload, attestation };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test end-to-end import validation in CI/CD?
- How should failed attestations be handled and remediated?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates practical experience architecting cross-cloud identity solutions, zero-trust controls, and incident readiness for a high-stakes data platform.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-cloud identity federation (IBM Cloud, Coinbase Cloud, Two Sigma)
- STRIDE/PASTA threat modeling methodology
- OAuth2/OIDC token lifecycle management with HSM signing
- Phishing-resistant MFA (FIDO2/WebAuthn, hardware tokens)
- Device attestation and mutual TLS
- RBAC/ABAC hybrid access control model
- Tamper-evident audit trails
- Incident response and testing: tabletop exercises, red-team drills

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo token validation sketch
async function verifyToken(token, publicKey) {
  try {
    const payload = jwt.verify(token, publicKey, {
      algorithms: ['RS256', 'ES256'],
      issuer: 'https://idp.example.com',
      audience: 'data-science-platform'
    });

    // Check token age
    const now = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);
    if (payload.exp - now > 900) { // Max 15 min
      throw new Error('Token lifetime exceeded policy');
    }

    // Verify device attestation claim
    if (!payload.device_trusted) {
      throw new Error('Device not attested');
    }

    return payload;
  } catch (err) {
    throw new AuthenticationError(err.message);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical CISSP logging, monitoring, and incident-response planning for distributed data platforms at a beginner level.

## Key Concepts
- Access control and RBAC
- Logging and monitoring
- Log integrity and tamper-evidence
- SIEM and alerting
- Incident tabletop and validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple log entry hash for integrity (illustrative)
const crypto = require('crypto');
function hashLog(entry, key){
  const h = crypto.createHash('sha256');
  h.update(JSON.stringify(entry));
  h.update(key);
  return h.digest('hex');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would data-residency rules affect log storage and access?
- What retention, deletion, and privacy controls would you implement for analytics logs?
